    "title": "Where did Artemis 2 land? how long has Artemis 2 been in space",
    "text": "NEWSWhere did Artemis 2 land? Artemis returns to Earth after 10-day mission Aaron A. BedoyaEl Paso TimesUpdated April 10, 2026, 6:51 p.m. MTThe Orion spacecraft has splashed down in the Pacific Ocean southwest of San Diego, ending Artemis II’s historic 10-day mission to the moon and back. Following liftoff on April 1, the 10‑day mission sent four astronauts on a flyby around the moon, testing life‑support, navigation and propulsion systems in deep space without landing, NASA said.Already a subscriber? Sign inTwo ways to continue readingPay Annually$119SAVE 50% versus MonthlySubscribeSubscribers getBEST DEALFull access to elpasotimes.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresMonthly$1for the first monthSubscribeSubscribers getFull access to elpasotimes.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresInterested in other subscriptions? Learn more",
